I immediately check the explanation for this error and reassure you: “This means the ID photo did not pass the clarity recognition. Please don’t submit it repeatedly for now. Retake it by following these steps:

1. Use the **original ID card** for the photo; do not use a screenshot, photocopy, or photo of a photo;  
2. Wipe the lens clean, take the photo somewhere with even lighting, turn off the flash, and avoid glare and shadows;  
3. Lay the ID card flat, make sure all four corners are fully in frame, the text and portrait are clear, and the image is not tilted;  
4. Upload the front and back sides separately as required by the page, and before submitting, confirm that there is no blurring or cropped edge;  
5. If it still fails, you can exit this page and re-enter it, and check whether the APP has been granted camera permission.

Please **do not send your ID card photo to the customer service chat window**. Retake it once according to the method above; if it still says failed, send me the error text or error code that does not contain ID information, and I’ll continue troubleshooting right away.”
